I fixed the last three yoyo-side parts of #1047 and committed it as 2f1b23f0. Clippy is clean, every cargo test suite passed, and tests/harness_logic.sh passed 212 of 212.

What changed
• Trust check at startup (src/config_paths.rs): reading the trusted-dirs store no longer hangs yoyo when the store is a FIFO. That store is checked before the first turn, so a FIFO there used to freeze yoyo with no message. Now it reads through non_regular_read::read_regular_to_string. If the store is a FIFO or device, the directory counts as "not trusted" and a warning on stderr says why. A missing store behaves exactly as before.
• Recording trust (--trust-project-always): this used to treat any read failure as an empty file and write over it. A FIFO hung, and a store with invalid UTF-8 was overwritten, losing every directory the user had trusted. Now only a missing store starts empty. A FIFO, a device or an unreadable store returns an error and the file is not touched.
  • I did not use read_for_rewrite as the task suggested. It still turns non-FIFO read errors into an empty string, which is the overwrite this store has to avoid.
• Module doc (src/non_regular_read.rs): the line saying yoagent's read_file trusts metadata.len() is out of date. yoagent 0.25.8 now refuses non-regular files in read_file, write_file and edit_file. The doc now says yoyo's tool wrapper is a second check, and that this module is still the only guard for yoyo's own startup readers. I added a version-claim marker.
• Other 0.25.7 mentions: I compared the 0.25.7 and 0.25.8 sources. The search, list and MCP code didn't change, so the claims in outside_read.rs, fence_result_filter.rs and ARCHITECTURE.md are still true and I left them as written.

Tests
• A FIFO store gives "not trusted", and recording trust refuses to write. Both run with a 10-second timeout, so a regression fails instead of hanging the suite.
• Near misses: a normal store still grants trust, a missing store is created exactly as before, and a store with invalid UTF-8 is not overwritten.
• I checked the FIFO test can fail: with the old bare read put back, it failed by name ("blocked on a FIFO (#1047): Timeout"). The code was restored and no marker is left.

Before the push
• Every mention of #1047 in src is a past-tense comment or test message, so none goes stale when the issue closes.
• A search of the startup code found three more unprotected reads that could hang on a FIFO. I filed them as #1052 and named it in the commit, so "Fixes #1047" stays true. I found these by reading the code and haven't run them against a real FIFO:
  • system_file in .yoyo.toml, read at startup (cli.rs:1005).
  • The session file restored by --continue (main.rs:1130).
  • The write_file diff preview (prompt.rs:633). It reads the old file before the tool runs, so yoagent's new refusal never gets a chance to fire.
• I left --system-file (cli.rs:2712) alone on purpose: the user types that path, and <(cmd) passes it a FIFO legitimately. #1052 explains why.
